  "synthesis": "None of the 13 items addresses neutrophils or NK cells as a primary subject, so the topic label does not match the retrieved literature. The records instead cluster around AI-driven and multi-omic characterization of tumor immunity. HistoProfile estimates CD8, FOXP3, PD-1 and PD-L1 densities from H&E whole-slide images, EcoNet models tumor microenvironment ecosystems for immunotherapy response, and NeoBridge reaches AUC-ROC 0.904 for pancreatic neoantigen prioritization. Clinical items include flow-cytometry tracking of 39 esophageal patients on anti-PD-1 neoadjuvant therapy and a serum SomaScan study in TNBC where GZMA is a candidate recurrence marker. Activity totals 10 published records and 3 preprints, with a rise ratio of 3.56 and no code, industry, or star signals. The items provide no basis for attributing this increase to a cause.",
